# Work and trade (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): everyday work talk most pairs can have. Few criteria, so almost
# any two who work together or near each other can draw on them; tagged lines let the trade, the till, the purse and
# the temper of whoever speaks colour each one. Specific scenes are in work7b.talk; prices and caravans in work7c.talk.

scene w7s_break_bread
when topic=work
a : Stop a moment. Here, half my bread. | Sit down, you're making me tired. | Is it break yet? Tell me it's break.
b[hungry=yes] : Gods bless you. I've had nothing since yesterday. | Gladly. My legs have been begging. | It's been break for an hour in my head.
b[tired=yes] : I'll not say no. I'll not get up again, either. | If I sit, I'll sleep. | Every hour's break, if you're tired enough.
b[temper=short] : Can't stop. Some of us work. | I'll sit when it's done. | No. And stop asking.
b : Go on, then. Just a crust. | A moment. Just one. | Near enough.
a : There. Now we're both slower. | Sit. The work's not going anywhere. | I'll take near enough.

scene w7s_late_in
when topic=work
a : You're late. | Where were you this morning? | Overslept again?
b[tired=yes] : Don't. I barely slept. | Lay awake half the night. | My eyes opened. My legs didn't.
b[parent=yes] : The pups. Always the pups. | One of the little ones was poorly. | Have you tried dressing three pups who don't want dressing?
b[humour=merry] : Late? I'm early for tomorrow. | I was here in spirit. | Overslept? I was resting my eyes. All night.
b : The road was full. | Errand for my mother. | Something like that.
a : Well, you're here now. | Don't let it be a habit. | Hm. Get on, then.

scene w7s_rude_customer
when topic=work
a : Had a customer this morning who sniffed everything and bought nothing. | One wanted it for half. Half! | A wolf shouted at me because it was raining.
b[role=merchant] : Every day. Every single day. | I'd have given them a quarter, and the door. | Blame the sky, but buy something.
b[warmth=warm] : Poor you. Some folk are just sour. | Some folk have no shame. | People need someone to shout at. Shame it's you.
b[humour=dry] : Was it me? I do that. | Half's a start. Did you ask for double? | Did you apologise for the rain?
b : Some folk. | The cheek. | Folk are strange.
a : Some folk indeed. | I sent them off. | I said I'd have a word with it.

scene w7s_lost_tool
when topic=work
a : Have you seen my good knife? | Who's had the hammer? It was right here. | Somebody's moved my things.
b[honesty=sly] : Not me. I mean, not today. | Hammer? What hammer? Oh, that hammer. | Moved? Tidied, I'd say.
b[humour=merry] : It ran off. Got bored of you. | Hammer's gone to find a better wolf. | Ghosts. The place is haunted.
b[temper=short] : I'm not your keeper. | Look with your eyes, not your mouth. | Nobody wants your things.
b : Where you left it, I'd think. | Under your elbow, maybe? | Not me. I've not touched them.
a : It's not where I left it. | ...Oh. Yes. Right there. | Someone has.

scene w7s_first_job
when topic=work a.stage=adult|old
a : Do you remember your first day at it? | What was the first job you ever had? | I was useless when I started. Truly useless.
b[stage=old] : Before your mother was born. I dropped a whole barrow of bricks. | Scaring crows for a penny a day. | We all were. The old ones laughed at me for a year.
b[stage=adolescent] : That was last month. I still remember. | This one. This is my first. | I still am, some days.
b[apprentice=yes] : I'm still on my first day, it feels like. | Sweeping. Still sweeping. | I am useless. My master says so.
b : I spilled everything I touched. | Carrying water, for a farmer who never paid. | Weren't we all.
a : And look at us now. | We've come up in the world. Slightly. | We get better. Or older.

scene w7s_other_life
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family|spouses
a : If you weren't doing this, what would you do? | Ever wish you'd learnt another trade? | What did you want to be, as a pup?
b[drive=restless] : Go to sea. Today, if I could. | Every day. Every single day. | Anything but this.
b[drive=content] : This. I'd still do this. | No. This suits me. | This, oddly enough.
b[drive=ambitious] : Own the place, not work in it. | I'll learn three more yet. | Rich. I still do.
b[stage=young|adolescent] : A guard! Or a sailor. Or a guard on a ship. | Is it too late? I'm only small. | I'm still a pup!
b : I'd have liked to be a scholar. Can't read, mind. | Some days. Most days I'm too tired to wish. | A guard. I liked the boots.
a : Not too late, maybe. | I'd swap. Some days. | Funny how it goes.

scene w7s_hiring
when topic=work
a : They're hiring at the yard, I hear. | Somebody's taking on paws down by the water. | Did you hear? The new shop wants help.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Where? Who do I ask? | What do they pay? I'll go today. | Tell me where. I mean it.
b[business=thriving] : I'll be hiring too, at this rate. | They'll not get mine, tell them that. | Good. Means trade's moving.
b[drive=restless] : Is it different work? I'd go for different. | Somewhere new. Tempting. | I'd go just for the change.
b : Good pay? | Who's asking? | Is it steady?
a : Less than you'd want. | A friend of a friend. | Steady as anything is.

scene w7s_wish_day_off
when topic=work a.working=yes
a : I'd give a week's #wages# for one day in the sun. | Wouldn't it be grand to do nothing at all? | I want to sleep for a whole Restday.
b[shift=day_off] : I'm doing it today. It's grand. | I am doing nothing at all. Look at me. | I'm going home to do just that.
b[tired=yes] : Don't. Don't make me think of it. | I'd sleep the whole day and the next. | I'd sleep two.
b[wealth=rich] : I could arrange that, you know. For me, I mean. | Nothing is overrated. | You'd be bored by noon.
b : Restday's coming. Hold on. | Now, wouldn't it. | Me too.
a : It's a long way off. | One day. | Dream with me.

scene w7s_compliment
when topic=work
a : That's good work, that. | You've a fine paw for it. | Did you do that? Neat as anything.
b[warmth=cold] : I know. | It'll do. | It's my job.
b[talk=quiet] : Oh. Thank you. | ...Thanks. | Mm. Yes.
b[humour=merry] : I know! I'm wonderful. Tell everyone. | Fine paw, fine wolf. | Neat as a new pin, me.
b : Thank you. Took me long enough. | Years of it. | I had to start it three times.
a : Worth it. | Shows. | Well, it shows.

scene w7s_mistake
when topic=work
a : I've done something stupid. | Don't look. I've ruined it. | If anyone asks, it was like that when I came.
b[warmth=warm] : Show me. We'll fix it before anyone sees. | Oh, come here. It's not so bad. | Your secret's safe.
b[temper=short] : Again? | What now? | I didn't see anything. And I'm not lying for you.
b[honesty=sly] : What's it worth to you? | Ruined? No. Creatively changed. | It was like that when you came. I saw it.
b : How bad? | Can it be mended? | Nobody'll notice.
a : Bad. | Maybe. With luck. | They'll notice.

scene w7s_paws
when topic=work
a : Look at my paws. Raw. | My pads are cracked to bits. | I've a splinter I can't get at.
b[job=healer] : Goose fat, twice a day. Don't argue. | Let me see. Hold still. | Out it comes. There. Don't cry.
b[stage=old] : Wait till they're forty years at it. | Mine stopped feeling anything years ago. | Here. My teeth are better than they look.
b : Rub some fat in. | Mine are the same. | Bite at it.
a : I'll try. | Small comfort. | I've been biting at it all morning.

scene w7s_fur_full
when topic=work
a : Look at me. I'm more dust than wolf. | My fur'll never be clean again. | I'll be combing this out for a week.
b[job=baker] : Flour. I sneeze bread. | Try flour. It gets in your ears. | Flour's worse. Trust me.
b[job=smith|miner] : Soot. I'm grey to the skin. | Coal dust in everything. | Grey's my colour now.
b[job=woodcutter|crafter] : Sawdust in my ears, sawdust in my supper. | Sawdust. It itches. | Shavings in my tail. Every night.
b[job=fisher|sailor] : Fish scales. They glitter, at least. | I smell of the catch. Folk move seats. | Salt. My fur's stiff as rope.
b : Roll in the grass on the way home. | Mine too. | A good shake helps.
a : The grass'll be dusty. | Small comfort. | I'll shake myself in the street.

scene w7s_whistle
when topic=work
a : *whistles* | *hums a tune, badly* | *sings under the breath*
b[temper=short] : Stop that. | If you do that once more. | Please. Anything else.
b[humour=merry] : *joins in, worse* | That's not how it goes. *sings it* | Louder! I can't hear the wrong notes.
b : Nice tune. | What's that one? | Do you know the one about the miller?
a : My mother's. | Old song. | Everybody knows it.

scene w7s_wages_secret
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends
a : What do they pay you, anyway? | Do you think we're paid fair? | Do you ever ask for more?
b[honesty=guarded] : That's my business. | Fair enough. Fair enough. | Not out loud.
b[honesty=frank] : Less than I'm worth, and I've told them so. | No. Nobody is. | Every month. Never get it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Not enough to eat on. | Fair? We're paid to stay hungry. | I'd ask if I thought I'd keep the job.
b : Enough to grumble. | Fair as anything is. | Once. Never again.
a : Hm. Same. | Fair as anything is, I suppose. | I know the feeling.

scene w7s_new_hand
when topic=work
a : There's a new one started. Have you met them? | New pair of paws here. Quick learner. | Who's the new face?
b[warmth=cold] : They'll not last. | Another mouth. | I don't learn names till they've lasted a month.
b[warmth=warm] : Lovely sort. I showed them where the water is. | Good. We need the help. | I'll take them under my wing.
b[stage=old] : Young. They're all young now. | Quick isn't everything. | I've seen dozens come and go.
b : Seen them. Seem all right. | Good. | Somebody's cousin, I think.
a : Give them a week. | We'll see. | We'll see what they're made of.

scene w7s_when_stop
when topic=work b.stage=old
a : When will you put your feet up, then? | You should let the young ones do this. | How long will you keep at it?
b[wealth=rich] : When I'm bored of #money#. Never, then. | They can do it when they can do it right. | Till I'm carried out.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : When I can afford to stop. Never. | Who'd feed me? | Till I drop. No choice.
b : When they bury me. | Young ones? They break things. | Till my paws give out.
a : Don't say that. | They learn. | Let's hope not soon.

scene w7s_pup_follows
when topic=work a.parent=yes
a : My pup wants to follow me into the trade. | Should I teach my little one the work? | Mine says they'll never do what I do.
b[stage=old] : Let them. It's a living. Or don't. It's a hard one. | Teach them. Then let them choose. | They all say that. Then they do.
b[drive=ambitious] : Aim higher for them. Much higher. | Teach them to read first. | Good. Push them up, not along.
b[parent=yes] : Mine wants to be a sailor. A sailor! | I'm teaching mine already. Slowly. | Mine too. Breaks my heart and mends it.
b : It's an honest trade. | Why not? | Pups change their minds.
a : Honest, and hard. | We'll see. | Every week, they do.

scene w7s_secret
when topic=work pair.band=friends|family|spouses|acquaintances
a : How do you get it so good? What's your trick? | There's a trick to it, isn't there. You're hiding it. | Show me how you do that.
b[honesty=frank] : No trick. Do it ten thousand times. | Practice. Boring answer, true answer. | Watch. Like this. Slower.
b[honesty=guarded|sly] : A trick? Me? | If I told you, I'd have to charge you. | It's a family secret. My family.
b : Patience, mostly. | There's no trick. Honest. | Watch closely.
a : I'll find out. | Hmph. | Like that? Oh. Oh!

scene w7s_leak
when topic=work here.weather=rain|storm|snow
a : The roof's leaking again. | There's a drip right over my bench. | Water's coming under the door.
b[wealth=rich] : Have someone see to it. | I'll send for a roofer. | Put a pail there. And then fix it.
b[role=merchant] : Move the stock before it spoils. | Not on the good cloth! | Don't let it near the goods.
b : Put a pot under it. | Shift your bench. | Sweep it out.
a : The pot's full. | There's nowhere to shift it. | It comes back.

scene w7s_omen
when topic=work
a : A crow sat on the roof all morning. I don't like it. | I dropped my bread butter-side down. Bad day ahead. | Saw a black cat by the door. Bad sign.
b[piety=devout] : Say a word to the gods and get on. | Signs are for the gods to read, not us. | Pray, and work. That's all.
b[humour=dry] : Crows like roofs. Also, crows are crows. | Bad day for the bread, anyway. | Bad for the cat, probably.
b[temper=nervy] : Oh no. Oh, I knew today felt wrong. | Don't say that. I'll fret all day. | That's twice this week!
b : Nonsense. | It's just a bird. | Cats go where they like.
a : We'll see. | Maybe. | I'll be careful anyway.

scene w7s_noise
when topic=work
a : What's that racket next door? | Someone's hammering like the world's ending. | Can you hear yourself think?
b[job=smith|crafter] : That's me, usually. | Sounds like honest work to me. | Not since I was ten.
b[temper=short] : I'll go and stop it myself. | Drives me mad. All day! | No. And it's their fault.
b : Building something. | Somebody's busy. | Barely.
a : Building what, a mountain? | Busy, or angry. | Let's shout, then.

scene w7s_smells
when topic=work
a : What's that smell? | Something's off. Can you smell it? | Gods, the stink today.
b[job=brewer] : That's the mash. You get used to it. Mostly. | Wort. Lovely stuff. | You call that a stink? Come by the vats.
b[job=fisher|cook] : That's yesterday's fish. Sorry. | Me, probably. | Fish. It's always fish.
b[job=crafter] : The tannery. Wind's turned. | Glue. Hot glue. | Lye. I'm boiling it.
b[job=farmer|herder] : That's me. Mucking out. | Honest dung. | Sheep. You never stop smelling sheep.
b : The drains. | Wind's from the yards. | Don't breathe through your muzzle.
a : Bless my nose. | Can't you shut it off? | I'll breathe through my ears, then.

scene w7s_sick_coworker
when topic=work pair.boss=no
a : Where's the other one today? | Half of us are off coughing. | Someone's taken sick.
b[job=healer] : I've seen them. They'll live. Tell them to stay home. | It's going round. Wash your paws. | Sweat it out, and keep it to themselves.
b[warmth=warm] : Poor thing. I'll take them soup. | I'll cover their share. | Let's send them something.
b[temper=short] : So we do their work too. Lovely. | Sick, or idle? | Always the same ones.
b : That cough's going round. | Better they stay away. | Hope it's nothing.
a : It's everywhere. | True. | Hope so.

scene w7s_gossip_boss
when topic=work pair.boss=no
a : The master's in a foul mood today. | Did you hear the boss shouting? | Watch yourself. Somebody's had bad news.
b[honesty=guarded] : I didn't hear anything. And neither did you. | Not my business. | Noted.
b[temper=nervy] : Was it at me? Was it about me? | Oh no. What did they say? | I'll keep my head down.
b[humour=merry] : Moods are like weather. Wait an hour. | I heard. The whole street heard. | Bad news? Somebody found the bill.
b : Again? | I'll keep clear. | Thanks for the warning.
a : Again. | Wise. | Spread the word.

scene w7s_strangers_trade
when topic=work|smalltalk pair.band=strangers
a : What's your trade, then? | You've a working look about you. What do you do? | Don't tell me. I'll guess your trade by the smell of you.
b[job=smith] : Smith. The soot gives it away. | Iron. Hinges, mostly. | Soot and hot iron. Go on, say it.
b[job=baker] : Baker. Flour on my muzzle, is there? | Bread. You'll have eaten mine. | Fresh bread, I hope you'd say.
b[job=fisher] : Fisher. You'll have smelt it. | Nets and boats. | Fish. Sorry.
b[job=farmer|herder] : I work the land. | Beasts and barley. | Earth and sheep, I'd bet.
b[role=guard] : The Watch. | I keep the peace. Mostly yours. | You'd better guess right.
b[role=merchant] : Buying and selling. | I keep a stall. Come by. | Nothing. I sell, I don't smell.
b : Bit of this, bit of that. | Whatever pays. | Go on, guess.
a : Good trade. | I'll remember. | Close enough.

scene w7s_friends_cover
when topic=work pair.band=friends
a : Cover for me this afternoon? Just an hour. | If anyone asks, I've gone for water. | I owe you for yesterday.
b[honesty=frank] : I'll not lie for you. But I'll not mention it. | You've gone for water. It's a very long well. | You do. And I'm keeping count.
b[warmth=warm] : Go on. I've got it. | Water. Right. Go. | You owe me nothing, #pet#.
b : One hour. | If they ask. | You do.
a : You're a treasure. | Bless you. | I'll pay you back.

scene w7s_family_business
when topic=work pair.band=family
a : Grandfather built this up from nothing. | It'll be yours one day, all of it. | Don't let it go to rack, when I'm gone.
b[stage=young|adolescent] : I'll make it bigger! | Do I have to? | When you're gone? Don't say that.
b[drive=restless] : Mine? I'd sell it and go. | We'll see. | I'll try.
b : I won't. I promise. | I know. | We'll keep it going.
a : Good. | You'll see. | I know you will.

scene w7s_spouses_work
when topic=work|family pair.band=spouses
a : How was it today, #dear#? | You smell of #work#, #dear#. | Leave it at the door, #dear#. Come in.
b[tired=yes] : Long. So long. Rub my shoulders? | I know. I'll wash. In a moment. A long moment. | I can't. It's followed me home.
b[business=failing] : Not good. We'll talk after supper. | Like a bad day. | Hard to leave it. We need to talk about the takings.
b[business=thriving] : Wonderful! We'll eat well this week. | Like money, I hope. | Gladly. It's been a good one.
b : Fine. Better now. | I'll wash. | Gladly.
a : Sit. I'll bring something. | Go on, then. | There.

scene w7s_rivals_customer
when topic=work pair.band=rivals
a : One of my regulars was seen at your door. | You've been undercutting me. Don't deny it. | Stop sending folk my way with lies about my prices.
b[honesty=sly] : Folk go where they like. | Me? I'd never. Not often. | Lies? I said you were dear. That's true.
b[temper=short] : Then keep them happy. | Prove it. | Watch your mouth.
b : Not my doing. | Prices are prices. | I've said nothing.
a : Hmph. | We'll see. | We'll see about that.

scene w7s_neighbours_work
when topic=work pair.neighbours=yes
a : Your hammering woke me at dawn. | I heard you working till midnight. | Your customers keep blocking my door.
b[warmth=warm] : I'm sorry. I'll start later. | Was I loud? Forgive me. | I'll ask them to mind it.
b[temper=short] : Your snoring wakes me every night. | Some of us need the #money#. | Then move your door.
b : Work's work. | Couldn't sleep. | Can't help where they stand.
a : I know. Still. | I know. | Hmph.

scene w7s_young_asks
when topic=work a.stage=young
a : What do you do all day? | Is your work hard? | Can I help? I'm very strong.
b[job=smith] : I hit hot iron till it gives up. | Hot and loud. You'd like it. | Stand back from the forge, then you can watch.
b[job=baker] : I make bread while you're asleep. | Floury. Want a crust? | You can shape a little loaf.
b[role=guard] : I watch for wrong-doers. Like pups who steal apples. | Only when there's trouble. | You can be my lookout.
b[temper=short] : Not now. | Go and play. | No.
b : Grown-up things. Dull things. | Sometimes. | Carry this. Carefully.
a : Sounds dull. | Is it? | I'm carrying it!

scene w7s_old_advice
when topic=work a.stage=old b.stage=adolescent|adult
a : Don't rush it. Rushing's how things break. | Measure twice. I learnt that the hard way. | Save a penny of every five. You'll thank me.
b[drive=ambitious] : Slow's for old wolves. No offence. | Twice? I'm faster than that. | A penny? I'll save two.
b[temper=short] : I know, I know. | You've told me. | I'll save when I've something to save.
b : I'll try. | Hard way? | I'll try that.
a : You'll learn. | Cut three planks short, once. | Good wolf.

scene w7s_tavern_after
when topic=work here.place=tavern
a : One cup, then home. | I'm not talking about work tonight. | First one's the best one, after a day like that.
b[tired=yes] : One. Before I fall asleep in it. | Good. I can't. | I'll drink it lying down.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : If you're buying. | Nor me. I'm talking about ale. | I'll watch you drink it.
b[shift=before] : I've not started yet! | I've not even begun. | Steady. Some of us start at dusk.
b : One, he says. | Thank the gods. | Every one's the best one.
a : One. Maybe two. | Not one word. | Every one.

scene w7s_street_load
when topic=work here.place=street
a : Mind your back, coming through! | Can you get the other end of this? | Out of the way, it's heavy!
b[temper=short] : Watch where you're swinging that! | Get a cart. | Go round!
b[warmth=warm] : Here, I've got it. | Lift on three. One, two... | Careful! Let me help.
b[stage=old] : My back's not up to it. Sorry. | I'll hold the door. | Watch your step there.
b : Mind yourself! | Go on. | Steady!
a : Sorry! | Thanks. | There!

scene w7s_market_shout
when topic=work here.place=market
a : I've been shouting since dawn. I've no voice left. | Nobody's stopping. They walk right past. | Somebody's set up right in front of me.
b[role=merchant] : Shout lower. It carries further. | They stop for a pretty pile. Stack it high. | Elbow them back out.
b[humour=merry] : Then sing it. Folk stop for singing. | Wave your arms. Stand on a crate. | Sit on their stall. See how they like it.
b : Rest it. | Be patient. | The cheek.
a : I'll try. | Patience doesn't sell. | Cheek's the word.

scene w7s_chapel_work
when topic=work here.place=chapel
a : Is it all right to talk of #work# in here? | Keep your voice down. They're praying. | The candles want trimming again.
b[job=priest] : The gods worked six days too. They'll not mind. | Thank you. Quietly does it. | I'll do them after prayers.
b[piety=devout] : Better to give thanks for it here. | Shh. | I'll help. It's good work.
b : Quietly. | Sorry. | I'll do it.
a : Quietly. | Shh. | Thanks.

scene w7s_field_work
when topic=work here.place=field
a : Rows and rows. My back's a bent nail. | Look at that sky. Will it hold? | Stones. This field grows stones.
b[job=farmer] : Every year I pull them, every year they're back. | It'll hold till dusk. After, who knows. | Bend your knees, not your back.
b[stage=old] : Sixty years I've bent in fields. Still here. | Ask my knees. They know. | Bent nails hold.
b : Keep at it. | Looks like rain. | Pile them at the edge.
a : Easy for you. | Looks like rain to me too. | There's a wall's worth.

scene w7s_shore_work
when topic=work here.place=shore
a : Tide's turning. | Gulls are thick today. Something's running. | My nets are tangled to the devil.
b[job=fisher|sailor] : Then we'd best be quick. | Mackerel, maybe. Get the boat. | Sit and mend. Nothing else for it.
b : I'll move my things. | Lucky birds. | Want a paw?
a : Quick, then. | Lucky me, I hope. | Please.

scene w7s_gate_work
when topic=work here.place=gate
a : Everyone wants through at once. | Carts backed up to the bridge. | Toll's gone up again, they say.
b[role=guard] : They'll wait. That's what gates are for. | Let them shout. I'm counting wheels. | Not my doing. I only take it.
b[job=carter|merchant] : And I'm one of them. | Mine's the third back. | Robbery. Every toll is.
b : Market day. | Slow going. | Is it?
a : Every day's market day here. | Slow as a sermon. | So they say.

## The seasons and days, for any two at work

scene w7s_spring
when topic=work here.season=spring
a : Days are drawing out. More work in a day now. | Spring. Everybody wants everything mended at once. | Mud everywhere. Spring mud.
b[job=farmer|herder] : Lambs and seed and no sleep. | Plough's waiting for me. | Mud's good. Mud grows things.
b[job=fisher] : The fish come up with the warm. | Boats need tarring. | Rivers high and brown.
b : More light, same pay. | Spring cleaning. | Mud in my boots.
a : Same pay. Always. | Never ends. | Mud in everything.

scene w7s_summer
when topic=work here.season=summer
a : Too hot to work. Too poor not to. | The flies! | Long days. I like the long days.
b[job=smith|baker|cook] : Try a forge in summer. | My oven's a second sun. | My kitchen's hotter than the street.
b[job=farmer] : Hay won't make itself. Sun's good for hay. | Flies on the beasts, flies on me. | Long days, long rows.
b : Take your coat off at least. | Wave your tail at them. | Too long, some.
a : Then my fur sweats. | Does nothing. | Not long enough.

scene w7s_autumn
when topic=work here.season=autumn
a : Harvest work for anyone who wants it. | Everyone's putting by for winter. | Nights coming in. Work's going dark.
b[job=farmer] : Then you'll lend a paw? | Every barn's bursting, gods be thanked. | Lamp oil's dear, too.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Where? I'll go. | I've nothing to put by. | I've no lamp oil.
b : Busy season. | Sensible. | I hate the dark mornings.
a : Busy, and gone too quick. | Like squirrels. | So do I.

scene w7s_winter
when topic=work here.season=winter
a : Can't feel my paws. | Work's thin in winter. | The ink froze in the pot this morning.
b[job=woodcutter] : Winter's my season. Everyone wants logs. | Wood's dear, and I'm cutting it. | Not mine. Felling's best when it's cold.
b[job=farmer|herder] : Feed and wait. That's winter. | Mending and worrying. | Ice on the troughs.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Thin work, thin soup. | Thin everything. | My paws froze to the cart.
b : Stamp your feet. | It'll pick up come spring. | Warm it by the fire.
a : I'm stamping. | Spring's a long way off. | What fire?

scene w7s_market_day
when topic=work here.day=market
a : Market day. Every wolf in the county's in town. | Have you seen the crowds? | Busiest day of the week, and I've a headache.
b[role=merchant] : Good. Let them spend. | Lovely. Lovely crowds. | Sell to it. A headache sells too.
b[role=guard] : Every cutpurse in the county too. | Watching them. All of them. | Mine's the crowds.
b[job=carter] : Carts nose to tail. I'll be all day. | Seen them? I've driven half of them. | Mine's from the road.
b : Market day, all right. | Hard to move. | Drink some water.
a : All right for some. | Like a herd. | Drink? Later.

scene w7s_restday
when topic=work here.day=rest
a : Restday, and here's us working. | Chapel bells, and I'm at my bench. | Everyone else is sleeping off the week.
b[piety=devout] : The gods will understand. I hope. | I'll go to evening prayers. | Not me. I'd rather pray.
b[role=guard] : Wrongdoers don't rest. Nor do we. | Restday's busy for the Watch. | Some of us never get Restday.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Rest doesn't feed me. | Bells don't pay. | Sleeping's for the comfortable.
b : Somebody has to. | Double pay, I hope. | Lucky them.
a : Always us. | Ha. Never. | Lucky them.

scene w7s_festival
when topic=work here.day=festival
a : The whole town's dancing and I'm stacking crates. | Can you hear the pipes? | Festival trade's good, at least.
b[role=merchant] : Best day of the season for the till. | Hear them? I'm selling to them. | Good? Wonderful.
b[job=brewer|innkeeper|cook] : They'll want feeding when the dancing's done. | Pipes mean thirst. | I've rolled out every barrel I own.
b : Finish quick and join them. | Lovely. | Some good, anyway.
a : Quick? Never. | Lovely to hear. | Something.

scene w7s_night_work
when topic=work here.time=night
a : Who works at this hour? Us, apparently. | The whole town's asleep but us. | Lamp's burning down.
b[role=guard] : The Watch does. Every night. | Not all asleep. Some are up to no good. | I'll walk you home after.
b[job=baker] : Bread starts at night. Always has. | They'll want loaves at dawn. | Dough doesn't sleep.
b : Odd hour. | Quiet, though. | Trim it.
a : Very odd. | I like the quiet. | Last one.

## The Houses, as anyone sees them

scene w7s_houses_own
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : Is there anything in Ridgemere the Houses don't own? | Everything I touch belongs to a House. | Brick's Greatly's, timber's Fell's, iron's Grayrock's. And me?
b[self.house=house_greatly] : Not much. Greatly owns the walls you're leaning on. | Greatly pays me. I'll not complain. Out loud. | You? You're Greatly's too, if you live in a brick house.
b[self.house] : My House pays on time. That's all I ask of it. | My House feeds me. I'll not bite the paw. | You're your own, if you're lucky.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : The dirt in the Sump. Nobody wants that. | Yes, and they let us look at it. | You're nobody's. Nor me.
b : The weather. They're working on it. | Feels that way. | Mossgrave's wool on your back, at least.
a : Give them time. | It does. | Ha.

scene w7s_greatly_rich
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
a : House Greatly's building again. Another wall. | They say Greatly's got more coin than the Crown. | Every new house in town is Greatly brick.
b[self.house=house_greatly] : And I'm the one carrying the bricks. | More than the Crown? More than sense. | Good brick, too. I'd know.
b[self.house=house_fell|house_grayrock|house_mossgrave] : Brick and paint. Showy stuff. My House makes what lasts. | Coin isn't everything. | Brick needs timber and iron. Remember that.
b[wealth=rich] : They're good neighbours to have. And to owe. | I'd believe it. | Sound brick, mind.
b : Walls and walls. | I'd believe it. | Somebody's getting rich.
a : Walls everywhere. | Wouldn't you? | Not us.
